# Secrets / credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
token.json
*.pem

# Intermediates — disposable, regenerated as needed (keep the dir, drop contents)
.tmp/*
!.tmp/.gitkeep

# Snapshot payloads: the raw page HTML and full-page screenshots.
#
# research/ is otherwise DURABLE and tracked on purpose — the dated snapshots
# are the baseline that month-over-month diffing compares against, and
# re-fetching cannot recover what a competitor's page said last month.
#
# But only the extracted .md and the .json metadata are needed for that:
# diff_snapshots.py reads the extracted text and the content hash, never the
# .html or .png. Those two account for 40MB of a 42MB repo and amount to
# republishing competitors' entire pages, so they stay local. Everything the
# pipeline and the evidence trail need is still committed.
research/snapshots/**/*.html
research/snapshots/**/*.png

# Print intermediate from `render_report.py --keep-html`. The PDF is the
# deliverable; this is just what Chromium consumed on the way to it.
research/reports/**/report.html

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
